From 3ded0d1d3348b9ad17838b1bfda4c1e9cbe1232c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Junod <donujp@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:06:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] displayid2: expose opt-in parsed capabilities on the
 0.3 ABI

Add four parsed-block accessors and their public interface-feature types
from the proposed parser API. Keep existing public type layouts, SONAME
and pkg-config version unchanged; require the new package revision for
new symbols and keep development/runtime versions matched exactly.

Restore native-only defaults in both legacy HDR/colorimetry getters.
Retain the earlier backport's explicit ordinary/nested first-match CTA
lookup, including complete CTA Type 1/luminance authority. An opt-in
Mutter consumer can use low-level native capabilities without silently
migrating existing callers through the old getters.

Exercise public getter ownership/fields, supported empty/audio children,
unsupported parent removal, diagnostics and block/extension order. Keep
all old-header fields and nested-CTA precedence covered. GCC analysis and
Clang ASan/UBSan pass39/39 before the final stronger removal assertion;
that focused requalification is pending. Only the synthetic native
print golden changes to the restored default.

This is a reviewed local proposal, not a released/accepted upstream API.
Packaging patch regeneration and final artifact qualification follow.
